{"id": "gap-88bce969dc", "d": "add", "leaf": "M2B.5.4/1", "page": "5:118:0", "mcq": {"s": "Match the following vitamins with the diseases caused by their deficiency:\nA. Vitamin A\nB. Vitamin D\nC. Vitamin C\nD. Vitamin K\n1. Scurvy\n2. Night blindness\n3. Excessive bleeding due to injury\n4. Rickets", "o": ["A-2, B-4, C-1, D-3", "A-4, B-2, C-1, D-3", "A-2, B-1, C-4, D-3", "A-3, B-4, C-1, D-2"], "a": 0, "x": "Vitamin A deficiency causes night blindness, vitamin D rickets, vitamin C scurvy, and vitamin K deficiency impairs clotting, causing excessive bleeding.", "src": "APPSC Assistant Motor Vehicle Inspector 2023"}}
